\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {subsection}{\numberline {4.2}H1: support-space cellular automaton on the 167-cycle}{6}{subsection.4.2}\protected@file@percent }
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces H1 update mechanics. (a) A stylized cycle view of the support state and the three-phase adjacent-swap schedule. Filled nodes indicate support bits equal to one; only \texttt  {01}/\texttt  {10} edges may swap, so weight is conserved exactly. (b) The fairness lock for the serious comparison: both \texttt  {parallel\_gain\_ca}{} and \texttt  {direct\_greedy}{} enumerate the same admissible swaps and score them with the same exact delta calculation. The only difference is the selection functional, which makes the later empirical comparison interpretable as a same-space test rather than a moving-target benchmark.\relax }}{7}{figure.caption.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:h1-mechanism}{{1}{7}{H1 update mechanics. (a) A stylized cycle view of the support state and the three-phase adjacent-swap schedule. Filled nodes indicate support bits equal to one; only \texttt {01}/\texttt {10} edges may swap, so weight is conserved exactly. (b) The fairness lock for the serious comparison: both \CA {} and \DG {} enumerate the same admissible swaps and score them with the same exact delta calculation. The only difference is the selection functional, which makes the later empirical comparison interpretable as a same-space test rather than a moving-target benchmark.\relax }{figure.caption.2}{}}
